Corresponding source for part 1 (how to get the complete source code)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The complete corresponding source of the exact binary in this archive is
published beside it on the same GitHub release page, as an
aria2-*-webui-*-sources.tar.gz asset.  It contains the patched aria2 tree, the
Web UI blob generator, the build scripts, the container images and the CI
workflow used to compile this binary — nothing else is needed to rebuild it.

That asset is generated from this repository, whose build recipe pins aria2 to
one exact upstream tag and commit; the values actually used are printed at the
end of THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt (section D) and in the release notes.  You can
also reproduce the tree yourself: see patches/README.md in the repository.

If you obtained this archive without its corresponding source and cannot
download it from the release page, open an issue at the repository above or
write to the address in NOTICE; a complete copy will be provided for at least
three years after this release.  That offer is a convenience — the primary
means of providing corresponding source is the release asset named above.
